 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Web push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send web push notifications to people's phones and desktops whenever something lands in their tray.
+To enable them, provide a VAPID key pair via the following environment variables:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` - the public key browsers use to subscribe to push notifications
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` - the private key Fizzy uses to sign push notification requests
+
+You can generate a key pair with the `web-push` gem that ships with Fizzy:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm --entrypoint bin/rails fizzy runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Without these keys, push notifications are disabled and people will still get their notifications in the tray and over email.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
